The arniko workspace ships ratatui 0.30 as a public dependency
(workspace `ratatui = "0.30"`). Round 6 catch-up mirrors the upstream
public Tabs surface verbatim so future consumers can reach the widget
through the `tornado` umbrella's `tabs` feature without taking a
hard path-dep on a vendored crate.

Local changes (intentional, minimal):

* Crate renamed `ratatui-widgets::tabs` -> `tornado_tabs` for arniko
  workspace cohesion (round 6 catch-up).
* Public type names preserved: `Tabs`, `TabsState`. The umbrella
  crate surfaces them through `pub use tornado_tabs as tabs` so
  callers may write `tornado::tabs::Tabs` (raw) or
  `tornado::widget::TabNav` (semantic alias) interchangeably.
* Path imports rewritten from the unstable 0.29-era
  `ratatui_widgets::*` subcrate split to the merged `ratatui::*` 0.30
  surface. (Round 9's `tornado-scrollview` applied the same migration
  from `ratatui-core`/`ratatui-widgets`; the public Tabs surface
  required no rewrite because 0.30's re-merge already published the
  public approach.)
* Six inline `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` smoke tests added under
  `tornado_tabs::tests::` — these exercise the public builder API
  surface and do not depend on any upstream tests. Upholds the
  round 6 directive "6 inline smoke tests".

License faithfulness:
  The dual-license text is preserved verbatim in LICENSE-MIT and
  LICENSE-APACHE at the root of this crate. The crate's
  `license.workspace = true` (MIT OR Apache-2.0) propagates
  arniko's umbrella license to consumers.

